te-author\">Ar.</span> <cite class=\"lex-cite-title\">Nu.</cite> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">344</span> </span>, <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <cite class=\"lex-cite-title\">Pl.</cite> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">385</span> </span>; <span class=\"gk\">μηδοτιοῦν</span> <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">Thgn.</span> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">64</span> </span>: rarely, <abbr>=</abbr> <b class=\"lex-tr\">whoever (whatever</b>), as subject of a verb, <span class=\"gk\">ὁτιοῦν ἔτυχε τῶν ἐπὶ μέρους</span> ( v.l. ὅτι ἄν ) <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">Arist.</span> <cite class=\"lex-cite-title\">Mu.</cite> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">391a22</span> </span>. </div> <div class=\"lex-sense\" data-level=\"4\"><span class=\"lex-n\">c</span> <span class=\"gk\">ὁστισδηποτοῦν</span> <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">D.</span> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">40.8</span> </span>, <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">Aeschin.</span> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">1.164</span> </span>. </div> <div class=\"lex-sense\" data-level=\"4\"><span class=\"lex-n\">d</span> so also <span class=\"gk\">ὅστις</span> alone, <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">Pl.</span> <cite class=\"lex-cite-title\">Hp.Ma.</cite> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">282d</span> </span>, etc.: with neg., <span class=\"gk\">μηδὲ οἵτινες</span> none <b class=\"lex-tr\">at all</b>, <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">X.</span> <cite class=\"lex-cite-title\">HG</cite> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">1.5.9</span> </span>; <span class=\"gk\">οὐδ' ἧστινος ἂν ἀσχολίας τὸ πρᾶγμα προσεδεῖτο</span> <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">Plb.</span> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">9.14.6</span> </span>. </div> <div class=\"lex-sense\" data-level=\"3\"><span class=\"lex-n\">3</span> <span class=\"gk\">ὅστις ποτε</span> <b class=\"lex-tr\">whoever</b>, <span class=\"lex-ci